  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607209910: Scaffold kotoba-lang/bmc — portable .cljc BMC canvas/ledger/gate/io core\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-20\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (+ Claude, standing new-project-scaffold authorization)\n\n## Context\n\nDuring worktree cleanup, four untracked `.cljc` files were found sitting in\nan abandoned git worktree on branch `feat/bmc-kotoba-lang-extraction`:\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/bmc/src/bmc/{canvas,gate,io,ledger}.cljc`. Per this\nsuperproject's `git-cleanup-conflict` retirement policy, WIP is never\ndiscarded outright — it was rescued to a pushed branch (commit\n`255a382537ecdd47ec3bc9829df7c80c0c7fa4ef`) with an explicit commit-message\ncaveat: \"Not yet a registered west project, no test coverage — needs owner\nreview before landing.\" This ADR records that owner review and its\noutcome.\n\nThe rescued code's own docstrings state its provenance unambiguously: it is\na **zero-product-literal extraction** of the same engine already running in\nproduction as this superproject's `70-tools/bmc` (`gftd.canvas` /\n`gftd.gate` / `gftd.ledger`, ADR-2607021500 / ADR-2607021600 / ADR-2607022100\n— the portfolio BMC/Lean-Loop CLI that operates cloud-itonami, cloud-murakumo,\nnet-kotobase, cloud-manimani, app-aozora, etzhayyim, and the `gftd` umbrella).\n`70-tools/bmc`'s own README already anticipated this exact split (\"将来分割:\n… 再利用部品 = com-junkawasaki 子リポへ split し、各 product repo の CLI から\ndeps 参照する\", ADR-2607021600). The rescued `bmc.*` namespaces strip out\nevery product/path literal that `70-tools/bmc`'s `gftd.*` binds concretely\n(base-datoms path, ledger path, gate-spec tables, layer-labels), leaving a\nreusable core: `bmc.canvas` (datoms index / event fold / md·text·EDN\nrender), `bmc.ledger` (append-only ledger read/append), `bmc.gate` (metrics\n-> hypothesis-status proposal evaluator), and `bmc.io` (a minimal `:cljs`\n(nbb) fs/env bridge, needed because nbb has no cross-repo `:deps`\nmechanism and this library cannot assume the workspace's shared\n`scripts/nbb_compat.cljs` shim is on the classpath when consumed\nstandalone).\n\nDuplication check performed before proceeding (per the standing\nnew-project-scaffold authorization's guardrail: confirm no conflicting\nreinvention of an existing production system before registering a new\nrepo, c.f. the BMC/Lean-Loop section of CLAUDE.md and its 2026-07-12\nnear-incident where a duplicate BMC tracking system was almost built from\nscratch). Reading both the rescued files in full and `70-tools/bmc`'s\nactual `.cljc` implementations (not just its README) confirms this is a\nlegitimate, non-conflicting companion library: it does not re-implement or\nshadow `70-tools/bmc`'s production behavior, it generalizes the same logic\nby removing product literals so it *could* eventually be depended on by\n`70-tools/bmc` (or any other product-bound CLI) instead of each script\nre-implementing canvas/ledger/gate logic per product. Nothing in\n`70-tools/bmc` has been rewired to depend on this library as part of this\nADR — that consumption wiring is deliberately out of scope here and is a\nfollow-up.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. Scaffold the rescued code as its own standalone west-managed project,\n   `kotoba-lang/bmc` (public, per repos.edn `:manifest.repos/orgs`\n   `kotoba-lang` role/scope and ADR-2607021330's org-visibility policy:\n   kotoba-lang = public) — **not** as files tracked directly inside\n   `com-junkawasaki/root`'s own git history. This matches the runtime/lib\n   placement convention already used for other portable `.cljc` `kotoba-lang`\n   libraries (e.g. `kotoba-lang/cron`, `kotoba-lang/crdt`, `kotoba-lang/crm`)\n   and the repo-naming rule against `-clj` suffixes (ADR-2607102200 addendum\n   14) — plain `bmc`, no suffix needed since the name was free.\n2. Repo content: `deps.edn` (zero third-party runtime deps, `:test` +\n   `:lint` aliases matching sibling `kotoba-lang` `.cljc` libraries'\n   convention), `README.md` (describes the library, its provenance, and the\n   no-test-coverage gap honestly), the four `.cljc` files unchanged under\n   `src/bmc/` (namespaces `bmc.canvas` / `bmc.gate` / `bmc.io` /\n   `bmc.ledger` already matched their file paths — no rename needed), and a\n   `.gitignore` matching sibling `kotoba-lang` `.cljc` libraries.\n3. Registered in `manifest/repos.edn` `:manifest.repos/extra-projects` as\n   `orgs/kotoba-lang/bmc`, and in `manifest/west.yml` via\n   `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry bmc` (minimal single-entry\n   diff, pin verified server-side against GitHub per ADR-2607022900).\n4. Known gap, explicitly accepted rather than fixed here: **no test\n   coverage**. The rescued code was scaffolded as-is; no tests were written\n   or fabricated as part of this ADR. This is a known, disclosed gap (see\n   the rescue commit's own caveat and the new repo's README \"Known gap\"\n   section), not an oversight — closing it is a follow-up for whoever\n   next depends on this library. The original commit's \"needs owner review\n   before landing\" condition is satisfied by this ADR: the owner-review\n   step is this scaffold decision itself, landing the rescued code as a\n   reviewed, registered, but still-untested standalone project rather than\n   leaving it stranded on an unregistered branch.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) The rescued WIP is no longer stranded on a branch nobody will\n  rediscover; it is a normal, west-registered, publicly-visible project.\n- (+) A reusable, zero-product-literal BMC/Lean-Loop core now exists as a\n  standalone dependency, available to `70-tools/bmc` or any other\n  product-bound CLI in the future without forcing an immediate, riskier\n  rewrite of the already-running production system.\n- (−) The library ships with zero test coverage. Anyone depending on it\n  should treat it as unverified WIP until tests exist.\n- (−) `70-tools/bmc` itself is not yet wired to consume this library — the\n  production system and this new library remain two independent\n  implementations of overlapping logic until that follow-up lands. This is\n  an accepted, explicit gap, not silent duplication (both this ADR and the\n  new repo's README document it and the shared provenance).\n\n## References\n\n- Rescue commit: `com-junkawasaki/root` `255a382537ecdd47ec3bc9829df7c80c0c7fa4ef`\n  on branch `feat/bmc-kotoba-lang-extraction`.\n- New repo: https://github.com/kotoba-lang/bmc\n- ADR-2607021500 (portfolio BMC/Lean-Loop base datoms), ADR-2607021600\n  (CLI/ReAct loop, source of the future-split note this ADR acts on),\n  ADR-2607022100 (gate evaluator design), ADR-2607021330 (org visibility\n  policy), ADR-2607171600 (docs/ADR EDN-only), ADR-2607173000 (nbb-only\n  script host).\n")))
